From d88302f93d833d7cad011bcf0103fdae75089aaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FAROVITUS <farovitus@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:38:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] graphics: composer 2.1 service stays on /dev/binder

On Android 17 my Galaxy S6 uses minigbm's AIDL allocator and the
stable-C mapper 5. libui loads mapper 5 only after servicemanager says
the AIDL IAllocator is declared, and vndservicemanager always answers
no. This service switched its process to /dev/vndbinder, so libui in
the HWC never saw the allocator, found no HIDL mapper either, and
aborted with "gralloc-mapper is missing".

Keep the process on /dev/binder. The composer itself still registers
over hwbinder; my HWC module starts no vndbinder services.

Change-Id: Id1cb1a6d9358855ed0417f2e27bfa13d5a570671
Signed-off-by: FAROVITUS <farovitus@gmail.com>
---
 graphics/composer/2.1/default/service.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/graphics/composer/2.1/default/service.cpp b/graphics/composer/2.1/default/service.cpp
index 1276d2df..6f595a03 100644
--- a/graphics/composer/2.1/default/service.cpp
+++ b/graphics/composer/2.1/default/service.cpp
@@ -28,8 +28,8 @@ using android::hardware::graphics::composer::V2_1::IComposer;
 using android::hardware::graphics::composer::V2_1::passthrough::HwcLoader;
 
 int main() {
-    // the conventional HAL might start binder services
-    android::ProcessState::initWithDriver("/dev/vndbinder");
+    // Stay on /dev/binder: libui finds the AIDL allocator, and with it
+    // mapper 5, only through servicemanager.
     android::ProcessState::self()->setThreadPoolMaxThreadCount(4);
     android::ProcessState::self()->startThreadPool();
 
-- 
